      "text": "Classic presentation: P, squeezing, or crushing chest discomfort, possibly radiating to the left arm, jaw, or back; associated diaphoresis, dyspnea, nausea, or vomiting. Any pt w chest discomfort or atypical Sx in an appropriate clinical context requires a 12-lead ECG w/in 10 min."
